Krita Nova 27 - the Brush Panel works with a finger while the pen is in use (Android)

While the pen hovers over or touches the screen, Krita's Android Qt does not
deliver finger touches to Qt as touch events (a finger that comes with the
pen's own motion events is lost in its tablet event). So the floating Brush
Panel could not be used with a finger while the pen was in use, whatever
palm rejection (patch 09) does.

1. MainActivity.java tracks the pen (touch and hover events) and, while it is
   in use (down, hovering, or used within the last second), reports finger
   touches to Krita through JNIWrappers.onPenTimeFinger (down / move / up /
   cancel, in pixels of the Qt view).
2. KisMainWindow.cpp, PanelFingerRouter: a reported finger that lands on the
   Brush Panel, its "more" popup or a popup opened from it is handed to the
   widget under it as mouse press / move / release. If the panel gets a press
   of its own within 80 ms (Qt delivered the touch after all, or patch 24
   forwarded it), the reported finger is dropped, so nothing is pressed
   twice. Fingers elsewhere are not used: the canvas keeps ignoring touches
   while the pen is in use.
3. The panel lookup shared with patch 24 (brushPanelWindowAt,
   belongsToBrushPanel) is now a pair of free functions.
